{"content":[{"c":["ZEMARAIM"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Town near the northern border of the territory of Benjamin (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.18.22","r":"Josh.18.22","rawR":"Josh.18.22","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.18.22","value":"Josh.18.22"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 18:22"},"). The most likely location is Ras ez-Zeimara, about five miles (8 kilometers) northeast of Bethel in the hill country between et-Taiyibeh and Rammum."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. Mountain in the hill country of Ephraim (",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.13.4","r":"2Chr.13.4","rawR":"2Chr.13.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.13.4","value":"2Chr.13.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 13:4"},") and the scene of Abijah’s speech of rebuke against Jeroboam and the Israelites."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Zemaraim","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Jos 18:22","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.18.22","rawQueryValue":"Josh.18.22","sourceRefExact":"Josh.18.22"},{"anchorText":"2 Chr 13:4","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Chr.13.4","rawQueryValue":"2Chr.13.4","sourceRefExact":"2Chr.13.4"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"504dd1b75767428a588885a06d88376d4d63c8f29099056a391f0b1982d3a64a","sourceItemName":"Zemaraim","sourceItemOrder":70,"sourceMember":"Articles/Z.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Zemaraim","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Zemaraim","title":"Zemaraim","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}